For nethack, the only possibility for multiplayer I think would be in
having a party system where messing with other members of the party or
their possessions would be verbotten. Any other way would make it
impossible. Loot could be a problem however. There could be problems with
stores - who goes in and do they only buy stuff for themselves and if not,
how to you manage to deal with scrolls destroyed when dropped for the
owner to pick up. There's probably numerous wrinkles like this that are
simple dealt with already in other computers RPG's. Nethack is one player,
one class take it or leave it I guess.


